{"agent_id":"pp3g-MKPL-exp7-t3a-scorer-metrics-core-zero-network-calls-read","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-09-29T14:24:05.629330447Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4ce2b6fe-caab-4f53-9a26-d55b1dcabc0e","comment_uuid":"120a52cc-6961-4d0a-80fd-8fb80f51feda","author":"pp3g-MKPL-exp7-t3a-scorer-metrics-core-zero-network-calls-read","content":"Plan: Exp7 T3a — deterministic scorer/metrics core (stdlib only, zero network calls, no measured Noul data exists yet).\n\n## Inputs (read-only, via git show — phase2 tree lives only on branch research/jev-phase1-565, absent from this worktree)\n- experiment7/DESIGN.md sections E (A/B/C measurements) and G (scorer correctness before measurement) — read in full.\n- experiment6/results/exec.jsonl (48 rows) — read-only comparator.\n- experiment6/analyze_stage6.py — pattern reference (pairing, aggregate/strata reconciliation, independent inline AUC recompute, rounded-to-4dp conventions).\n- experiment6/harness/score.py _auc/_overlap/_quantiles — convention reference (index-based quantiles; that convention is why Exp6 median is 0.36 while a mean-of-two-middles median is 0.345).\n- experiment7/run_noul.py (T2, on its own branch) — confirms the record shape I must consume: parsed == {type:'noul', noul: float in [0,1]}, qid=='sufficiency', keys case_id/pair_id/variant/ctype/qid.\n\n## Comparator vectors re-derived by me from Exp6 exec.jsonl (all match the brief)\npooled AUC (U-positive on p_ins) 0.8785 | ordering p_ins(U)>p_ins(A) 24/24 | delta min +0.05 mean +0.3908 (index-convention median 0.36) | false-unknown at frozen 0.05: polymorphic_dispatch 0/8, runtime_conditioned_reachability 8/8, runtime_target_selection 1/8 | A-correctness 19/24 | per-stratum AUC 1.0 x3.\n\n## Deliverable 1 — experiment7/analyze.py, built in THREE persisted+import-verified increments\nPART 1 parsing + pairing + section E.A\n - parse_rows: JSONL, required keys, qid pinned to the single frozen Noul, variant in {U,A}, parsed.type=='noul' with numeric non-bool noul in [0,1]; typed_error rows rejected; ZERO rows is a hard failure.\n - scorable guard written as SEPARATE checks, never one compound 'and' — DESIGN section G explicitly requires historical short-circuit rejection.\n - pair_rows: group by pair_id, exactly one U and one A per pair, ctype agrees, no orphan rows, exactly 24 pairs / 48 rows.\n - E.A: ordering rate (A>U) with reversals and ties counted separately, all 24 deltas, min/median/mean overall and per stratum, secondary two-sided exact sign test (ties excluded, alpha 0.05) by exact integer arithmetic.\nPART 2 section E.B + E.C\n - E.B: pooled AUC A-positive on p_suff, per-stratum AUC, U/A distribution overlap, min/median/p90/max quantiles per variant, per-class median baseline shifts.\n - E.C: frozen-Choice comparator with U-positive orientation on p_ins, plus the oriented comparison table carrying q_ins = 1 - p_suff labelled transform-only. Hand-checkable identities asserted: AUC flips under score reversal; q_ins delta is numerically identical to the p_suff delta.\nPART 3 run_selfcheck()\n - nine mechanical checks: polarity, AUC hand fixture + inverted rejection, aggregate==strata, pairing, cardinality incl. real nonzero exit on zero rows, variant identity (incl. row-order invariance), independent delta recompute, comparator orientation, short-circuit rejection. Each check runs against SYNTHETIC hand-computable fixtures; the Exp6 known-answer vector check runs against the read-only comparator file.\n\n## Deliverable 2 — experiment7/SCORER-PROOF.md\nPer-check expected/actual, every fixture written out so a reader can recompute by hand, the Exp6 known-answer vector table, the negative-control (mutant) list with which were caught, and the honest statement of what was NOT tested.\n\n## Constraints honoured\nNo network calls of any kind. No thresholded analysis of measured Noul data and no code path that could perform one — the only threshold in the file is the FROZEN Exp6 0.05, read for comparator-only reproduction, never applied to Noul values. No answer-accuracy claim about the Noul; Exp6 19/24 appears only as a reproduced context comparator. No answer content is read. experiment6/, packet files and run_noul.py untouched. Commit only analyze.py and SCORER-PROOF.md.\n\n## Certainty\nEvidence-based: DESIGN E/G read verbatim, Exp6 vectors re-derived by me from the raw rows and confirmed against stage6_findings.json. NOT TESTED: any real Noul value (none measured) and the empirical behaviour of the Noul primitive — out of scope until the freeze gate.","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:24:05.619670035Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:2tAOcFujJk9CXAmtLr8QZ9F3jXP6zpK5NBzv+t6L0E4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgXTjKghXflYWUBWD+Y27V0O/kb1JjXAOSu8b7cvZZbB8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAlHI5sKzs3mx8FqL3tYbKdiareMuUeOsWqLAzgWAhC+IGkO6Hu2Ehl/pItLoiUSCkku6zpkbtxTrRDMSOzgQwBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:2tAOcFujJk9CXAmtLr8QZ9F3jXP6zpK5NBzv+t6L0E4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgXTjKghXflYWUBWD+Y27V0O/kb1JjXAOSu8b7cvZZbB8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH5R7MKVRgZPVkie5KBak/SJ9omWKTIytfuspXnNU2qoP4xD4kRFc/c40dcanEypkFaaD/ETFM8nLka4ZsgY9wE="}
