{"agent_id":"pp3g-MKPL-exp7-t3a-scorer-metrics-core-zero-network-calls-read","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-09-29T14:42:39.073475918Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4ce2b6fe-caab-4f53-9a26-d55b1dcabc0e","comment_uuid":"1e3debd6-eca5-4f39-9e57-30454aa98855","author":"pp3g-MKPL-exp7-t3a-scorer-metrics-core-zero-network-calls-read","content":"Result: Exp7 T3a scorer/metrics core COMPLETE. analyze.py (2207 lines) + SCORER-PROOF.md committed as cd12df0d7; total 4 commits on this branch, containing exactly the two authorized paths and nothing else.\n\n## Built in three persisted, import-verified increments\n6f4dcf806 part 1 (parse + pair + E.A) -> import OK -> 5d404f41e part 2 (E.B + E.C comparator) -> import OK -> 9b199de46 part 3 (selfcheck) -> cd12df0d7 (proof doc + final fixes).\n\n## E.A primary (DESIGN 92-97)\nOrdering / reversal / tie counted SEPARATELY so a reversal cannot be described as a win. All 24 paired deltas p_suff(A) - p_suff(U), min/median/mean overall and per stratum. Secondary two-sided exact sign test, ties excluded, alpha 0.05, computed with math.comb over 2**n in integer arithmetic -- 24/0 gives exactly 2/2^24 with no float drift.\n\n## E.B (DESIGN 99-103)\nPooled AUC A-positive on p_suff, per-stratum AUC, U/A overlap, min/median/p90/max per variant, per-class median baseline shifts and cross-class median range. No threshold, no operating point, no tuning.\n\n## E.C (DESIGN 105-116)\nFrozen Exp6 read through its OWN record shape (a Choice row carries parsed.probabilities plus an answer key; a Noul row carries parsed.noul and none), so the two primitives can never be scored through the same path. Comparison table stated in one shared frame (positive = insufficient) via q_ins = 1 - p_suff, transform_only + note on all 7 rows. quantiles reproduces the frozen Exp6 INDEX convention exactly -- this matters: Exp6's median is 0.36 under the index rule and 0.345 under mean-of-two-middles, so an unpinned estimator would have made the E.C table compare two different estimators and reported the difference as a finding about the Noul.\n\n## Exp6 known-answer vectors: all reproduced from raw rows, 0 mismatches\nAUC 0.8785 (inverted 0.1215) | ordering 24/24 | deltas min +0.05 median 0.36 mean +0.3908 | false-unknown at frozen 0.05: 0/8, 8/8, 1/8 | A accuracy 19/24 | per-stratum AUC 1.0 x3. I re-derived all ten figures with an ad-hoc script BEFORE writing any scorer code, so these are confirmations rather than transcriptions.\n\n## Self-check: 11/11 PASS, exit 0, and PASS under python3 -O\npolarity | auc hand fixture | aggregate==strata | pairing | cardinality + zero-case nonzero exit | variant identity | independent delta recompute | comparator orientation | short-circuit rejection | no-threshold-on-noul | known-answer-is-live.\n\n## Negative control: 15 injected defects, 15 CAUGHT, 0 survivors\nEach run in a fresh process. The first run was 13/15 and BOTH survivors were real gaps in my suite, not harness noise: (a) the quantile check only tested self-consistency, so a mean-of-two-middles mutant passed while silently breaking comparability with Exp6's 0.36 -- closed with two hand-counted estimator fixtures; (b) check_known_answer was never CALLED by any check, so a neutered gate passed -- closed by a check that requires it to reject six single-field corruptions. Had I stopped at 'all checks pass', both would have shipped.\n\n## Seven real defects found in my own code while writing the checks\nThree would have survived an imports-and-runs check: summarize_discrimination keyed per-class breakdowns on the global STRATA tuple instead of the strata present, so the ENTIRE per-stratum E.B path raised KeyError; the E.C table computed the oriented AUC as to_q_ins(1 - auc), applying the reflection twice and reporting the NATIVE value in the q_ins column; reconcile() called with the wrong arity. Also: a wrong hand count on a tie fixture (0.75 for 0.875), two fixture spreads pushing probabilities outside [0,1], a 'bad value' fixture using 0.5 which is LEGAL, and a dict unpacked as a tuple. All fixed. I also recorded an editing error rather than hiding it: a tool call failed schema validation and the fallback append omitted a signature rewrite.\n\n## The two absences, discharged mechanically not in prose\nE.D no-threshold: a SOURCE AUDIT reads this file's own source, strips comments, and fails on any p_suff comparison against a numeric literal. 0 hits. The only threshold literal is the frozen Exp6 0.05, applied solely to already-measured already-frozen Choice rows, with provenance recorded in the emitted report.\nE.E correctness firewall: structural. The Noul path never reads an answer key; 19/24 is Exp6's CHOICE accuracy, computed by the separate Exp6 reader the Noul path cannot reach, and labelled context-only in the report.\n\n## Constraints honoured\nZero network calls: module imports only json, os, sys, math.comb (plus a local re/tempfile inside two checks); no socket, no subprocess, no credential. Two consecutive analyze runs byte-identical. No second Noul formulation (qid pinned; any other refused -- mutant 14). Pairing by pair_id label, never position (reversing all 48 rows gives a byte-identical report). experiment6/, packet files and run_noul.py untouched -- verified across ALL FOUR commits, not just the working tree. Every fixture synthetic; the only real data read is the read-only Exp6 comparator.\n\n## ENVIRONMENT CAVEAT (unchanged, still operator-gated)\nThe phase2 tree, including experiment6/results/exec.jsonl, exists only on branch research/jev-phase1-565 and is NOT in this worktree, so all such inputs were read via 'git show research/jev-phase1-565:<path>'. The known-answer command was pointed at a git-show extract. This branch can never be merged into research/jev-phase1-565 by me: merge and push are both operator-gated. Merging feature/pp3g-MKPL-exp7-t3a... into research/jev-phase1-565 is still required for these artefacts to land next to experiment6/.\n\n## Certainty\nEvidence-based, high confidence for the MECHANICAL properties: every check was executed rather than reasoned about, and the 15/15 is a measurement. NOT TESTED, stated in full in SCORER-PROOF.md section 8: no measured Noul value exists, so nothing here says anything about H1 or H2; the real results/exec.jsonl schema is assumed from run_noul.py and never exercised against a real record; the Exp6 0.05 was not re-read from packet.json this session; and the Noul/Choice semantic equivalence question is not addressed and must not be.","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:42:39.065842666Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:2tAOcFujJk9CXAmtLr8QZ9F3jXP6zpK5NBzv+t6L0E4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgXTjKghXflYWUBWD+Y27V0O/kb1JjXAOSu8b7cvZZbB8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAuFrFmPp5UYioM60JUfWOs/BHKvNb0ENHZOd7O/4yN58JRgVAlF6rT4icKe47RxJ/7diiMP6hMUSV1MP56nGBAw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:2tAOcFujJk9CXAmtLr8QZ9F3jXP6zpK5NBzv+t6L0E4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgXTjKghXflYWUBWD+Y27V0O/kb1JjXAOSu8b7cvZZbB8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQE5HVIvInDNYtBBnYURNqKHYLkyRfqxygO1UJdAByP3pVbwrWKPAxVd2ze+/nkFp4unI/dnwZ70JtYJ4gbv4cg4="}
